stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> TurnStart

    TurnStart --> Approach: gap needs closing
    TurnStart --> Windup: already adjacent lane

    state Approach {
        [*] --> Closing
        Closing --> Closing: multi-lane close (per skill range)
    }

    Approach --> Windup: reaches target lane

    state Windup {
        [*] --> Real
        [*] --> Fake
    }

    Windup --> Attack: Real windup resolves
    Windup --> Approach: Fake resolves — reposition beat follows

    Attack --> ReturnToOrigin: timed input resolves (hit or guarded)
    ReturnToOrigin --> Complete: hop-arc animation completes

    Complete --> [*]

    note right of Approach
        Sequences are fully committed once started.
        No voluntary bail-out, no external interrupt —
        Root/Stun/Reaction skills do NOT cut a
        sequence short (decided this pass — no prior
        directive locked Approach as an interrupt point).
        Beat list authored per skill, e.g.
        [Approach, Windup-Fake, Approach,
        Windup-Real, Attack]
    end note

    note right of ReturnToOrigin
        Origin lane recorded once, at sequence start.
        Return always targets that single value,
        regardless of how many Approach/Teleport
        hops occurred mid-sequence.
    end note
